## Why This Is Asked
Tests integration of pose and shape estimation with active perception under strict latency. Pushes on-device adaptation for unseen tools and robust uncertainty handling.

## Key Concepts
- Next-best-view planning for pose disambiguation
- Uncertainty-aware pose and mesh estimation
- On-device meta-learning for 5-shot adaptation
- Differentiable rendering losses and domain randomization

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: forward pass outline
function forward(x){
  const z = encoder(x);
  const pose = poseHead(z);
  const mesh = meshHead(z);
  const depthLike = render(pose, mesh);
  return {pose, mesh, depthLike};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify NBV gains without ground-truth future views?
- Which ablations most impact 60 ms frame-time on typical edge GPUs?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates robust multi-hand 3D pose with fine-grained articulation under occlusion, plus on-device adaptation for real-world diversity.

## Key Concepts
- 3D hand pose (finger joints), hand mesh (MANO)
- Temporal tracking and occlusion handling
- On-device few-shot adaptation and edge latency

## Code Example
```javascript
function totalLoss(key3d, pred3d, mesh3d, predMesh3d, tio, contactPred, contactGT){
  const lKey = mse(key3d, pred3d);
  const lMesh = l2(mesh3d, predMesh3d);
  const lTemp = mse(pred3d, tio);
  const lContact = crossEntropy(contactGT, contactPred);
  return 0.4*lKey + 0.3*lMesh + 0.2*lTemp + 0.1*lContact;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate hand-object contact reliability in clutter?
- What ablations would you run to isolate the impact of articulation accuracy vs. contact estimation?
